WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Reading the interaction graph.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
An arrow means the source species appears in the target species rate of change.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
A positive partial derivative is green activation; a negative partial derivative is pink inhibition.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
A self-arrow means autoregulation. Pure first-order turnover, minus k times X, is not drawn as a self-edge.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Influences below five percent of the strongest influence on a target are folded from the readable view.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Show all connections reveals folded influences as thin dashed edges.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The graph is a readable view. The Equations tab is always complete.
